RED_EVIDENCE_GET_DISPLAYS_CORRUPTION (both a rejected envelope and a quarantined record are DISPLAYED, not aborted; the quarantined original is shown verbatim at records[1] and json status=corrupt; controls: absent still renders "not configured" and clean still renders "configured", neither carrying the corruption marker)
RED_EVIDENCE_ADD_REPAIRS_WITHOUT_LOSS (round trip: corrupt artifact -> red_evidence_create -> re-read; the malformed original is still on disk byte-identically at records[1], the repair record is appended, no derived quarantine key is persisted, and the next read quarantines the same entry again; the un-restored append is shown LIVE to lose it; an unreadable envelope is refused with "Nothing written" and a repair command, writing nothing; control: the clean write path is unchanged)
EVERY_CONSUMER_DISTINGUISHES_CORRUPTION_FROM_ABSENCE (9/9 consumers re-derived by symbol: handlers/proofstory.ts red_evidence_get; handlers/proofstory.ts red_evidence_create; handlers/proofstory.ts diagnosticInput (proofstory_gate_check); handlers/phase-gates.ts REVIEW completeness gate; handlers/phase-gates.ts DONE intent-equivalence gate; core/machine.ts proofStoryDevGateFailure; handlers/red-evidence.ts findV2Record; handlers/red-evidence.ts red_evidence_binding_set; handlers/story-review.ts story_review (C3 advisory path) — each names the corruption for BOTH a rejected envelope and a quarantined record, each differs from its own absent-artifact output, and none marks an absent or clean artifact; C3: the story_review advisory path renders "CORRUPT" and no longer renders "unavailable")
